    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a disposable-email-domain blocklist that rejects `POST /api/owners` with a **400** when the owner's email domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\nFiles added:\n- **`RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java`** \u2014 a validation step reading the body via `@Val`; email is optional (null/blank passes through), and it throws when the domain is on the blocklist.\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `InvalidEmailException`).\n- **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- **`...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml`** \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\nFiles changed:\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `rejectDisposableEmail` step right after `normalizeEmail`, so the domain is already syntax-validated and lower-cased before the blocklist check.\n\nThe new acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
